A||||4||ChadMan||Lost a close one to a mulletmobile||||10||
Z||000000||ChadMan||04-05-2001||10:14 AM||||Coming home from work last night on Riverside Drive, I found myself with the pole position at a red light.  A '75 or '76 Cutlass Supreme rolls up next to me...he's got loud dual exhausts, a lumpy-idling V8 and is moderately jacked-up in the back.  It's got a little body cancer, but not a bad-looking car overall.  Can my 88 Coupe take him?  We'll see...<P>I know his lane ends about 1/8 mile past the intersection, so I know he'll launch hard to try and beat me to the merge.  Sure enough, when the light turns green, he punches it and I hear his duals bark and his tires chirp, but I made one of the best launches ever and beat him out of the hole nice and clean.  When I shift to second I've got a couple of carlengths on him, but now his V8 is roaring, that big sled has some momentum built up and he's pulling alongside.  When I grab third, he slowly draws ahead and it's all over...I have to back off at the merge and let him go on by.  At least he was cool about it and didn't "gloat" by creeping along at 10 mph under the limit to irritate me after he won.<P>I'm sure the guy was surprised that a 4-banger gave him such a close run, but that's little consolation.  Losing sucks.  I hope I do better at the autocross track than I do racing mullets on Riverside Drive.||||reg||10
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||04-05-2001||11:41 AM||||Ah - you would have taken him if you had a V6... sounds like you *still* gave him a run for his money though. 4-cyl vs. V8? Good job...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
